{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"dee5434939165bbba583648e05e7810a3ecd58823b0173c90063f8ce88822544","packTokens":3517,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":627,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":742,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1827,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace the current manual processes with a single platform covering stock, orders, deliveries, live temperature monitoring, quality decisions and recalls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a responsive web portal for warehouse staff, dispatchers, quality staff, administrators and auditors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a customer portal for hospitals, pharmacies and clinics.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a driver experience that keeps working without a connection.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Receive temperature readings from data loggers and cold-room sensors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep a centralized shared record of stock, orders and temperature history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Support secure sign-in, role and warehouse access controls, customer-organization isolation, and read-only auditor access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Define versioned product temperature profiles and stability budgets.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Receive stock by lot, track inbound logger readings, quarantine stock, and release it through quality review.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Let customer users place, view, change and cancel orders under the specified delivery and order rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Allocate released stock to orders by earliest expiry while respecting shelf-life, availability and order-completion rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Pack stock into qualified shipper boxes and plan routes with drivers and vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Store and process delayed, duplicated and out-of-order temperature readings reliably.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Detect excursions, charge stability budgets, place affected stock on hold, and alert relevant users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Enable drivers to load, drive and record delivery handovers using their phone, including offline use.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Support the portals in English and Arabic, with Arabic displayed right to left.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Track recalled lots, block remaining stock and account for customer responses.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What must the full two-person quality decision for stock exposed to a not-permitted temperature range require?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Quality Officer proposes the disposition and a different Quality Manager approves it; neither person can perform both steps.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When an excursion opens, how quickly must affected stock be placed On Hold relative to the alert deadline?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Place it On Hold as soon as the excursion is detected; the two-minute deadline applies to alerts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What customer evidence must the driver record for a delivery handover?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record the recipient's name and an explicit electronic acknowledgment of receipt; a drawn signature is not required.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to quantities that are not handed over because a delivery is refused or only partly completed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep undelivered quantities outstanding; record the reason and return them to available stock only after warehouse receipt and any required quality checks.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What constitutes a handling unit for tracking stability budgets when a received quantity is split, moved, or packed into different boxes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Track quantities as handling units and split the record whenever portions acquire different temperature histories.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain a customer organisation's saved delivery addresses and minimum remaining shelf-life requirement?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customer Administrators maintain their organisation's addresses; System Administrators set its minimum shelf life.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the stock quantity breakdown reconcile with quantity on hand, given that stock can also be On Hold, Rejected, Recalled or Expired?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat on-hand as the total and show a mutually exclusive breakdown that includes available, allocated, quarantined and the other stock statuses.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When a product profile changes with an effective date, how should the new profile affect stock already received and its temperature-budget history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the new version to stock still held from its effective date onward and recalculate affected budgets and decisions from that date.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build the Meridian as a responsive web app with role-oriented portal pages and navigation for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls across phone, tablet, and desktop browsers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff sign-in through Meridian Microsoft accounts and customer sign-in through email, password, and a one-time code, with email reset links and no customer social sign-in or single sign-on.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Show users only records and actions returned for their role, assigned warehouses, or customer organisation; make Auditor views read-only and clear protected data when access is refused.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Let Customer Administrators invite and remove users within their organisation, and maintain its saved delivery addresses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Let System Administrators list, search, view, deactivate, and maintain products; set an organisation's minimum remaining shelf life; and create versioned temperature profiles with storage bands, contiguous non-overlapping tiers, allowance or not-permitted designations, reason, and effective date, while earlier versions remain read-only.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Show API-returned recalculated budgets, decisions, and current stock, order, box, and route statuses when profile versions take effect, including backdated changes, affected allocations, and any returned action requirements or handover restrictions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let Warehouse Operators record receipts with product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, cold room, and shelf; upload inbound logger files and separate image or PDF evidence files; and show returned quarantine status, temperature readings, and budget use before release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Let quality staff review receipts and excursions, present available release or disposition actions, and show API-returned decisions, including separate proposal and approval steps for not-permitted-range dispositions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Show on-hand stock with separate returned quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired statuses, plus warehouse, lot, product, receipt, location, and handling-unit details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Provide stock-movement forms and show returned source and destination locations, quantity, actor, and time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Show the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life value read-only to customer users and Dispatchers, and let customer users create orders with product lines, pack quantities, saved delivery addresses, eligible delivery dates, and partial-or-complete delivery preference.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned eligible delivery dates and warehouse time zone, prevent ordering deactivated products, and provide complete order summaries before submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Show order status and allocated and outstanding quantities per line; provide customer change and cancellation controls only before Packed and dispatcher cancellation controls when returned as available; display API outcomes and prevent duplicate submissions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Show order allocations by line and lot with expiry dates and quantities, provide dispatcher lot overrides with a required reason, and show returned allocation, stock-status, box, and route outcomes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Let Warehouse Operators pack stock into shipper boxes by type, associate one logger with each box, and show returned compatibility, contents, quantities, and sealing details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Let Dispatchers create and view routes with date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times; show confirmation errors, configured qualified-duration safety margins, route changes, schedules, and driver-notification status returned by the API.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Show temperature histories for boxes, cold rooms, and lots in chart and table views, including returned readings, applicable bands, excursions, gaps, flags, and silence status; identify readings excluded from calculations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned excursions, affected handling units, tier-budget use and remaining allowances, alerts, hold statuses, decision statuses, review cases, and stock statuses without estimating temperatures or charging unobserved tiers for unresolved history gaps.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an installable, responsive driver web experience that caches the current workday's assigned route, queues supported loading and delivery actions for later synchronization, shows returned synchronization and stale-route outcomes, clears cached route and delivery data on sign-out, workday end, or disabled-account response, and retains unsynchronized actions for another synchronization attempt or returned rejection.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Let drivers record delivery handovers with recipient name, explicit electronic acknowledgment, handed-over quantities, and any refusal or partial-delivery reason; show outstanding quantities and returned delivery status, and show returned warehouse receipt and quality status for returned stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Let Quality Managers start recalls by selecting affected lots and entering a reason, view and manage recall records, and close recalls; let customer users submit quantities and stated dispositions for each affected delivery, and show returned reconciliation, outstanding quantities, affected responses, and blocked-stock information.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Provide filtered on-screen operational lists and CSV export, and show creator and last-changer identities and timestamps as read-only metadata where returned.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Provide English and Arabic portal content, rendering Arabic pages right to left and English pages left to right.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure every portal page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch targets of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels on phone layouts; conform main staff, customer, and driver flows to WCAG 2.1 Level AA.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the stated first-year user and record volume and simultaneous device volume.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}